11. Write a program that implements a Hangman-style word guessing game. The
game should allow a player to guess letters of a hidden word, track incorrect
guesses, and display progress. The program should store a list of words in a
prepopulated array, list, or similar. A random word should be selected as the
target word for the game.
During the game, display the word with unguessed letters replaced by
underscores (_). Prompt the player to guess a letter. Check if the guessed letter is
in the word: If correct, reveal the letter in the word. If incorrect, track the wrong
guess and reduce remaining attempts. Display the current state of the word and
the number of attempts left.
Maintain a list of previously guessed letters to prevent duplicate inputs. The
player wins if they guess all letters in the word. The player loses if they exceed the
maximum number of incorrect guesses (e.g., 6).
At the end, display the correct word and a win/loss message.


